course: dictionary
lesson: 10965
title: Names of peoples and places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wampanoag is a name, so it starts with a capital letter. It is the name of a Native American people, a group who share a homeland, a language and a history. «In 1621 the Pilgrims and the Wampanoag people shared a harvest feast.» The words «the Wampanoag people» tell you that Wampanoag names a group, not one person.
explain: The rest of the sentence gives you more clues. «The Wampanoag had helped the settlers survive by teaching them to grow corn.» To survive means to stay alive, and corn was the food that helped them do it. So the Wampanoag were the helpers, the people who taught the settlers.
explain: Wampanoag can also describe things that belong to that people, as in Wampanoag language. Their language is also called Wôpanâak. Some words have more than one meaning, so check which one fits. In the sentence above, the Wampanoag are a people, so the first meaning is the right one.
fact: Wampanoag is a noun for a Native American people, and it is also the name of their language.
fact: The Wampanoag lived in what is now Massachusetts and Rhode Island, in the USA.
fact: «Settlers» means people who come to live in a new place.
fact: The Pilgrims arrived on the Mayflower in 1620, and the Wampanoag helped them survive.
fact: The Wampanoag still live in that area today.
exercise: «In 1621 the Pilgrims and the Wampanoag people shared a harvest feast.» What is the Wampanoag? | *A people, a group of Native Americans | A type of food, like corn | A ship that sailed across the sea | A feast held once a year in winter
exercise: «The Wampanoag had helped the settlers survive by teaching them to grow corn.» What did the Wampanoag do for the settlers? | They sent them home | They built them a castle | They sailed them across the sea | *They taught them to grow corn
exercise: The Wampanoag language is also called Wôpanâak. In «the Wampanoag language», what does Wampanoag mean? | A lake in Massachusetts | A kind of ship | *Their language | A harvest feast
test: Which word is a name, so it needs a capital letter? | corn | *Wampanoag | settlers | feast
test: Which area did the Wampanoag live in? | California and Oregon | Texas and Florida | Maine and Vermont | *Massachusetts and Rhode Island
exam: Which word in «the Wampanoag people» tells you that Wampanoag names a group? | *people | the | shared | Wampanoag
